IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-70, TARGETED: the Purchase Tax (Goods and Services) Law, 5712-1952 ("the Law"; the English title is a working translation of the Hebrew title the amending instruments print). Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records two references of the Law (items I1 and I2) as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: the dealer or importer to whom the list of Customs Ordinance provisions (I1) or of Value Added Tax Law provisions (I2) is applied for the purchase tax. A row of references asks that individual no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: a provision cited by a list, an instruction of an amending instrument, one step of replaying instructions on a list, a citation of a list, and the questions asked of them. No reference is stated here; they are in pc70-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Every item is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument read.
--
-- LATIN LETTERS. The Hebrew of every number and quoted word is on an `ext:` line (read from the deposited page image of an official instrument) or a `src:` line (the deposited excerpt of the consolidation), and the modules type it in Latin letters (tools/translit.py checks the Latin against the Hebrew, line by line):
--   the prefix vav with maqaf is written `and-`; the word between two numbers that means "up to" is written ` to `;
--   alef, bet, gimel, dalet after a digit are A, B, C, D (29C is 29 gimel, 144A is 144 alef); alef, bet, gimel in brackets are (a), (b), (c).
-- THE NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's. A status is what the instruments READ give; the row says nothing about a provision no instrument read touches except that none was read. NotChecked is a value, not an absence: it marks a number a list names that this row did not read.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `A status in the instruments read` IS ONE OF
    Repealed
    Added
    NotChecked

DECLARE `How a limb was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page image`
    `official page images, with the absence of a later instrument resting on the consolidation's tag list (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`

DECLARE `A kind of instruction` IS ONE OF
    Replace
    `Insert after`

-- A provision of another law that a list of the Law cites, or that an instrument read adds.
-- `the day the pages read print for the status to begin` is NOTHING wherever the pages read print no day: an issue date is not a day of effect.
DECLARE `A provision` HAS
    `the law it belongs to` IS A STRING
    `its number, with letters in Latin` IS A STRING
    `its status in the instruments read` IS A `A status in the instruments read`
    `the instruction that gives the status` IS A STRING
    `the issue date printed on the instrument that gives the status` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day the pages read print for the status to begin` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `what the status rests on` IS A STRING

-- An instruction of an amending instrument that edits a list of the Law, as the page prints it.
-- `the words it quotes first` are the words replaced, or the words after which it inserts; `the words it quotes second` are the words that come in.
DECLARE `An instruction` HAS
    `the instrument and item` IS A STRING
    `the issue date its footer prints` IS A DATE
    `the section of the Law it names` IS A STRING
    `its kind` IS A `A kind of instruction`
    `the words it quotes first` IS A STRING
    `the words it quotes second` IS A STRING

-- One step of replaying the instructions on a list, applied LITERALLY: the quoted words are looked for in the text, nothing is added or removed except the quoted words, and no separator is supplied.
-- When the quoted words are not in the text, the instruction does not apply to it literally and the text is unchanged (that is a fact about the replay; the row does not say what a reader does then).
DECLARE `A replay step` HAS
    `the instruction` IS A `An instruction`
    `the text before the step` IS A STRING
    `the text before the quoted words` IS A STRING
    `the text after the quoted words` IS A STRING
    `the quoted words are in the text before the step` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the text after the step, applied literally` IS A STRING
    `the tokens after the step, with punctuation ignored` IS A LIST OF STRING

DECLARE `A list citation` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the section of the Law that holds the list` IS A STRING
    `the tokens of the list as first printed` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the tokens of the list after the instructions read` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the provisions the row checked` IS A LIST OF `A provision`
    `the provisions the row did not read` IS A LIST OF `A provision`
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- The questions. Each takes a value from pc70-cross-references.l4.

GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision is repealed by an instrument deposited here` MEANS p's `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS Repealed

GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision is not repealed by an instrument deposited here` MEANS NOT (p's `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS Repealed)

GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision is added by an instrument deposited here` MEANS p's `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS Added

GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision was not read` MEANS p's `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS NotChecked

GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A STRING
`the number of the provision` MEANS p's `its number, with letters in Latin`

GIVEN c IS A `A list citation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many provisions the row checked in the list are repealed` MEANS count (filter `the provision is repealed by an instrument deposited here` (c's `the provisions the row checked`))

GIVEN c IS A `A list citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no provision the row checked in the list is repealed` MEANS NOT (any `the provision is repealed by an instrument deposited here` (c's `the provisions the row checked`))

GIVEN c IS A `A list citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold` MEANS c's `limb (a) holds` AND c's `limb (b) holds`

-- The shape of a step: the text before it splits into the words before the quoted words, the quoted words, and the words after them.
GIVEN s IS A `A replay step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the text before the step is its three parts joined` MEANS s's `the text before the step` EQUALS CONCAT (s's `the text before the quoted words`), (s's `the instruction`'s `the words it quotes first`), (s's `the text after the quoted words`)

-- A replacement puts the second quotation where the first was; an insertion keeps the first and puts the second after it.
GIVEN s IS A `A replay step`
GIVETH A STRING
`the text a replacement gives` MEANS CONCAT (s's `the text before the quoted words`), (s's `the instruction`'s `the words it quotes second`), (s's `the text after the quoted words`)

GIVEN s IS A `A replay step`
GIVETH A STRING
`the text an insertion gives` MEANS CONCAT (s's `the text before the quoted words`), (s's `the instruction`'s `the words it quotes first`), (s's `the instruction`'s `the words it quotes second`), (s's `the text after the quoted words`)

-- The day a repeal began is not given by the pages this row reads (the printed date of an issue is not a day of effect), so the answer is NOTHING for every provision.
GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the repeal of the provision began, as the pages read print it` MEANS p's `the day the pages read print for the status to begin`
